---
source: crates/clattertrap-cli/tests/help.rs
expression: "String::from_utf8(out.stdout).unwrap()"
---
Build Rube Goldberg machines with AI models and watch whether they work

Usage: clattertrap <COMMAND>

Commands:
  rules   Print the rules contestants play by, or a JSON Schema
  levels  List every level with its tier and goal
  level   Describe one level in words and JSON
  check   Validate a scene file against its level; exits 1 with the problems
  look    Write a PNG of a scene at the start of its run
  run     Run a scene to its end and print the outcome as JSON
  arena   Run a Claude model through the contestant tools and save every run (the pilot)
  report  Summarize a directory of pilot runs: levels solved per model and arm, attempts, and exclusions
  mcp     Serve the contestant tools over stdio as an MCP server
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version
